---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { BUSINESS, INDEPENDENCE, LAST_UPDATED } from "../lib/site";
---

<Page
  title="Terms of use and sale | Waymark"
  description="The terms that apply when you use Waymark and when you buy full access."
  heading="Terms of use and sale"
  updated={LAST_UPDATED}
>
  <p class="note">Payments are not open yet. These terms describe how sales will work at launch.</p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Waymark is run by {BUSINESS.legalName}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>. Our
    address is on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. {INDEPENDENCE}
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Waymark is</h2>
  <p>
    Waymark is a study tool for the Life in the UK test. Our questions are original practice items based on the official
    handbook (3rd edition). They are not real test questions, and we cannot guarantee that any question will appear in
    your test. Our readiness estimate is based on your practice and is not a promise of a result.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Free and paid access</h2>
  <p>
    You can use part of Waymark for free. Full access is a one-off digital purchase. It is not a subscription and does
    not renew. The price is shown before you pay and includes any taxes that apply.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How long access lasts</h2>
  <p>
    Full access lasts for the current edition of the official handbook (3rd edition), for as long as that edition is
    used for the test. If a new edition is introduced within 12 months of your purchase, you will get the new-edition
    content at no extra cost.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your right to cancel</h2>
  <p>
    Because full access is digital content you can use straight away, you will be asked at checkout to agree that access
    starts immediately and that you then lose the usual 14-day right to cancel. See
    <a href="/refunds">cancellation and refunds</a> for what we offer, and our <a href="/pass-promise">pass promise</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. If something goes wrong</h2>
  <p>
    If the content is faulty, you have rights under the Consumer Rights Act 2015, including repair or replacement and,
    in some cases, a refund. Tell us at <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.support}`}>{BUSINESS.support}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Using Waymark fairly</h2>
  <p>
    Your access is for your own personal study. After you pay, you get an unlock code that works on up to 3 of your own
    devices (for example your phone, laptop and tablet). Please don't share it with other people. If you replace a
    device, email us and we will reset your code. Please don't copy, resell or republish our questions or explanations.
    Organisations can buy access for others: see <a href="/for-organisations">Waymark for organisations</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Our responsibility to you</h2>
  <p>
    We work hard to keep every question accurate and fix reported errors quickly. We are not responsible for losses
    that were not foreseeable, for decisions about your immigration status, or for the official test fee. Nothing in
    these terms limits your legal rights as a consumer.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The version shown when you buy applies to that purchase.</p>

  <h2>10. Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. If you live in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you can also
    bring a claim in your local courts.
  </p>
</Page>
